Original commit body from 93b6ff9e96d2eacb8922ed4ce914465eaeefddef:

§9 carried the complete eight-base entrypoint confidence list. §8's tier table
carried four of them and closed "All four confidence tiers are now implemented."
§12 asserted the four "span [0.70, 0.99]" and that the only other values sat
below that band. Both of the latter are false against the detector: 0.90, 0.80
and 0.75 sit inside [0.70, 0.99] and are none of the four, and the omitted 0.75
library_export is — by §9's own measurement, twelve hundred lines away — the
most common entrypoint kind on this repo's corpus (45 of 118). WI-logad fixed
one copy of the table and left the other two standing.

§8's table is now the canonical eight rows and says so; §12 stops enumerating
and records what it previously got wrong; 0.05 is named as a suppression
sentinel below MIN_ENTRYPOINT_CONFIDENCE (0.10), not as a tier.

Two more hand-maintained numbers, same class:

Symbol.meta's registered-key count was three short — §9 said 47 where
meta_keys_on_axis(AXIS_SYMBOL_META) returns 50.

§3's io-boundaries entry advertised "150+ framework IO entries" for catalogues
ADR-0016 rules stdlib-only ("the stdlib-only catalog scope is sound and stays").
The claim predates the strict-stdlib cull that removed third-party rows by a
month, and it was unfalsifiable as written: entries carry module/methods/notes
and no stdlib-vs-framework marker, so the number could not be checked even in
principle. Replaced with the scope rule and the census that is checkable.

Guarded by test_spec_ir_contract.py: §8's table and §9's list must each equal
the set of confidence= literals the detector emits, read from the AST. A regex
over entrypoints.py also matches the three confidence=0.9x mentions inside
_detect_from_concepts's docstring — which is how the first pass at this finding
over-counted emit sites (41; actually 38) and briefly mistook that function's
accurate per-family docstring for a fourth competing model. A vacuity control
asserts all three extractors still match, so equality cannot pass on empty sets.
Verified by differential: reverting either defect fails the guard naming it
(missing [0.75]; spec says 47, registry has 50).

